NAME
       w - show who is logged in and what they are doing

SYNOPSIS
       w [-h] [-s] [USER]

DESCRIPTION
       w starts with the same line as uptime (time, time up, users, load
       average), then lists each login session: user name, terminal (TTY),
       where the user came from (FROM: an address for ssh logins), when they
       logged in, how long they have been idle, the CPU time used, and the
       command they run now (WHAT). With USER, only that user's sessions.

OPTIONS
       -h     Leave out the header lines.

       -s     Short format: leave out the login time and CPU columns.

EXAMPLES
           w
           w student

SEE ALSO
       who(1), uptime(1), users(1), last(1)
